00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:05,440
Treaty Feasibility and Cost Analysis Previous treaties failed because they ran on guilt.

2
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:14,280
Guilt has terrible fuel efficiency. This one runs on greed, which is (regrettably) humanity's only reliable fuel source.

3
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:19,380
"Getting one hundred and ninety-five countries to agree costs billions and takes forever.".

4
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:26,980
No. Getting countries to implement things costs billions. Getting them to sign papers is surprisingly cheap.

5
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:34,540
Humans love signing papers. It makes them feel important. Your entire diplomatic system runs on the principle that writing

6
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:37,460
your name on a document feels like accomplishing something.

7
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:43,570
Sometimes it is. Usually it isn't. But the signing part is always affordable.

8
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:53,340
What Treaties Actually Cost. Non-governmental organization, or N.G.O., campaign budgets are rarely disclosed publicly, but

9
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:57,040
treaty campaigns run on pocket change compared to the thing they create.

10
00:00:57,580 --> 00:01:05,880
The Ottawa Treaty banning landmines took fourteen months. One staff member, Jody Williams, grew a coalition to over a thousand

11
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:11,500
organizations across sixty countries. One hundred and twenty-two states signed.

12
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:19,000
She won the Nobel Peace Prize. One woman with a phone convinced one hundred and twenty-two countries to stop burying explosives

13
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:26,680
in the ground where children walk. Your species is capable of remarkable things when one person gets sufficiently annoyed.

14
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:34,300
The Cluster Munitions Convention took about two years. Seven governments and a coalition of N.G.O.s got ninety-four states

15
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:39,440
to sign. The Arms Trade Treaty took a decade but started with three supporting governments.

16
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:45,840
The Control Arms coalition published more than fifty reports until one hundred and thirty countries signed.

17
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:54,940
The Nuclear Ban Treaty also took a decade. I.C.A.N., the International Campaign to Abolish Nuclear Weapons, ran the entire

18
00:01:54,940 --> 00:02:01,400
operation with five staff in a Geneva office. One hundred and twenty-two states voted yes.

19
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:07,430
Another Nobel Prize. Five people in a Geneva office won a Nobel Prize.

20
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:16,100
You have more people in your accounting department. Pattern: Total to get a treaty signed: fifteen to fifty million dollars.

21
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:20,160
Your species spends more than that on Super Bowl ads for beer.

22
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:28,560
Beer. The thing that makes you temporarily stupider. You will spend more money selling stupidity beverages during one sporting

23
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:33,060
event than it costs to get one hundred and twenty-two countries to agree on anything.

24
00:02:33,620 --> 00:02:39,580
I've been watching your species for eighty years and the budget comparisons still surprise me.

25
